## 💻 Installation and Setup

### Step 1: Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/himanshu-verma/random-dog-image-generator.git
```

### Step 2: Open the project folder

```bash
cd random-dog-image-generator
```

### Step 3: Create a virtual environment

```bash
python -m venv venv
```

### Step 4: Activate the virtual environment

For Windows:

```bash
venv\Scripts\activate
```

### Step 5: Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Step 6: Run the application

```bash
streamlit run main.py
```

The application will open in your default web browser.

## 📖 How to Use

1. Open the Random Dog Image Generator.
2. Select a dog breed or choose All Breeds.
3. Click Generate Random Dog.
4. Wait for the dog picture to load.
5. View the generated dog image.
6. Click Download Dog Image to save it.

## 🐕 API Endpoints Used

| Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/breeds/list/all` | Get all available dog breeds |
| `/breeds/image/random` | Get a random dog image |
| `/breed/{breed}/images/random` | Get a random image of a selected breed |
| `/breed/{breed}/{sub-breed}/images/random` | Get an image of a selected sub-breed |

